WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:03.450
- Hello, I'm Anthony Abeson.

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:04.449
I'm an acting coach.

00:00:04.449 --> 00:00:08.032
I've been doing it for,
wow, over 30 years.

00:00:08.883 --> 00:00:11.725
Today we're gonna be working
with a few non-actors.

00:00:11.725 --> 00:00:13.758
We're gonna give them
emotional result pressure.

00:00:13.758 --> 00:00:15.244
We've created one line.

00:00:15.244 --> 00:00:17.454
"I'm sorry, I didn't mean
to get so emotional,"

00:00:17.454 --> 00:00:19.371
which is pretty clearly

00:00:20.755 --> 00:00:23.635
a demand that you get emotional.

00:00:23.635 --> 00:00:25.892
Just to make it even more diabolical,

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:30.038
we're gonna ask them
to first try to produce

00:00:30.038 --> 00:00:32.621
that emotional result
without any help from me.

00:00:32.621 --> 00:00:33.782
- Red leather, yellow leather.

00:00:33.782 --> 00:00:34.885
Red leather, yellow leather.

00:00:34.885 --> 00:00:37.218
Red leather, yellow leather.

00:00:38.075 --> 00:00:39.594
(sighs)

00:00:39.594 --> 00:00:40.818
- I'm sorry.

00:00:40.818 --> 00:00:44.317
I didn't mean to get so emotional.

00:00:44.317 --> 00:00:45.763
- I'm sorry.

00:00:45.763 --> 00:00:48.596
I didn't mean to get so emotional.

00:00:52.246 --> 00:00:54.913
(loud thudding)

00:00:56.665 --> 00:00:58.991
- Sorry, I didn't mean
to get so emotional.

00:00:58.991 --> 00:01:00.378
- I'm sorry.

00:01:00.378 --> 00:01:03.211
I didn't mean to get so emotional.

00:01:06.051 --> 00:01:08.129
- I really didn't mean
to get that emotional.

00:01:08.129 --> 00:01:10.796
(coughs softly)

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:14.704
- I didn't mean to get so emotional.

00:01:15.687 --> 00:01:17.770
(laughs)

00:01:20.923 --> 00:01:22.506
This is so awkward!

00:01:24.162 --> 00:01:27.203
- [Anthony] So who's the most
important person in your life?

00:01:27.203 --> 00:01:28.715
You don't even have to say who it is.

00:01:28.715 --> 00:01:29.548
- Okay.

00:01:29.548 --> 00:01:30.926
- I'm from New York City,

00:01:30.926 --> 00:01:34.521
so paying bills is a big thing for me.

00:01:34.521 --> 00:01:37.047
Just being able to pay
my rent and my bills,

00:01:37.047 --> 00:01:39.803
so I guess that'd be really
sad if I couldn't do that.

00:01:39.803 --> 00:01:42.877
- [Anthony] Would you tell me
a little bit about your mom?

00:01:42.877 --> 00:01:45.741
- My mother is a teacher,
or was a teacher.

00:01:45.741 --> 00:01:47.141
She's a retired teacher now.

00:01:47.141 --> 00:01:48.174
- [Anthony] Do you love her?

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:49.329
- Yes.

00:01:49.329 --> 00:01:52.135
- As a kid, the idea of having to give

00:01:52.135 --> 00:01:54.719
the love of a dog away is just really sad.

00:01:54.719 --> 00:01:57.812
- [Anthony] So could you picture
them over here somewhere.

00:01:57.812 --> 00:02:01.979
And could you just very softly
say to them, "I love you"?

00:02:04.684 --> 00:02:05.517
- I love you.

00:02:05.517 --> 00:02:07.585
- I love you, mom.

00:02:07.585 --> 00:02:08.699
- [Anthony] Did you ever have a dog?

00:02:08.699 --> 00:02:09.615
- I did.

00:02:09.615 --> 00:02:10.649
- [Anthony] What was his name?

00:02:10.649 --> 00:02:12.538
- His name was Dude.

00:02:12.538 --> 00:02:13.434
- [Anthony] What kind of dog?

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:15.794
- He was a little Corgi,
Pembroke Welsh Corgi.

00:02:15.794 --> 00:02:18.431
Ate nothing but cheeseburgers
and chicken nuggets.

00:02:18.431 --> 00:02:19.539
- [Anthony] What happened to him?

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:20.656
- My parents had to put him down

00:02:20.656 --> 00:02:22.232
while I was working at a music festival.

00:02:22.232 --> 00:02:23.611
- [Anthony] What would
be the scariest thing

00:02:23.611 --> 00:02:25.571
about being homeless?

00:02:25.571 --> 00:02:27.213
- I'd be afraid of being beaten up,

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:30.640
or getting taken advantage
of by people on the street.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:34.807
- [Anthony] I'd like you to
picture a really scary guy

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:40.051
who's looking at you.

00:02:40.051 --> 00:02:41.258
Do you worry about them?

00:02:41.258 --> 00:02:42.238
- Yes.

00:02:42.238 --> 00:02:43.349
- [Anthony] Would you
just worry about them

00:02:43.349 --> 00:02:45.140
for a moment, please?

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:49.239
(suspenseful synthesizer music)

00:02:49.239 --> 00:02:50.489
- It's intense.

00:02:52.273 --> 00:02:54.771
- [Anthony] And he's coming closer to you.

00:02:54.771 --> 00:02:57.172
And he's a big, huge, scary guy.

00:02:57.172 --> 00:02:58.422
- [Jade] Mm-hm.

00:02:59.995 --> 00:03:02.057
- Dude, I miss you.

00:03:02.057 --> 00:03:05.456
I'm sorry I couldn't be there for you.

00:03:05.456 --> 00:03:07.456
And that I was so close.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:12.563
But, yeah, that you
had to pass without me.

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:17.285
(melancholic guitar music)

00:03:17.285 --> 00:03:18.541
I'm sorry that your last years

00:03:18.541 --> 00:03:21.291
you didn't get to see much of me.

00:03:23.612 --> 00:03:24.862
But I love you.

00:03:26.396 --> 00:03:30.563
- [Anthony] What could happen
to them that you worry about?

00:03:34.481 --> 00:03:36.981
There they are in their coffin

00:03:37.859 --> 00:03:41.442
and would you just very
softly say goodbye?

00:03:43.061 --> 00:03:44.159
- Goodbye.

00:03:44.159 --> 00:03:45.076
I love you.

00:03:47.324 --> 00:03:48.564
- [Anthony] Say the line, "I'm sorry.

00:03:48.564 --> 00:03:51.564
"I didn't mean to get so emotional."

00:03:52.817 --> 00:03:54.367
- I'm sorry.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:57.200
I didn't mean to get so emotional.

00:03:58.542 --> 00:03:59.918
- Sorry.

00:03:59.918 --> 00:04:02.501
I didn't mean to get emotional.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:07.962
- I'm sorry, I didn't
mean to get so emotional.

00:04:07.962 --> 00:04:11.879
- I'm sorry, I didn't
mean to get so emotional.

00:04:13.556 --> 00:04:15.110
- [Anthony] You started
to believe a little bit?

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:17.053
- [Benjamin] Mm-hm.

00:04:17.053 --> 00:04:18.106
- [Anthony] Remember no bad juju.

00:04:18.106 --> 00:04:20.027
- [Benjamin] Mm-hm.

00:04:20.027 --> 00:04:22.851
- It really took me back
to this sensational place

00:04:22.851 --> 00:04:24.970
of feeling the weight of his paws

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:27.505
and feeling how his belly felt

00:04:27.505 --> 00:04:29.948
that it really kinda allowed
me to connect with that moment.

00:04:29.948 --> 00:04:32.007
- I'm more in touch with
my feelings right now.

00:04:32.007 --> 00:04:36.768
Just thoughts of different
images, different smells.

00:04:36.768 --> 00:04:38.851
- I really felt helpless.

00:04:40.626 --> 00:04:42.464
Yeah, with no family, no friends,

00:04:42.464 --> 00:04:46.631
and that is completely the
opposite of everything that I am.

